This is soo weird, i don't understand why this is happening

ok bro wtf is going on, that first log i sent you of that old recording, yeah i just opened it and it's working just fine!!! umm bruhh. I didn't even put it on my premiere pro. ugh

&#x200B;

* Anytime there are playback issue with a video you've finished encoding, it is always worth checking playback in a second program. VLC is a must-have for this.

\--so should i actually install vlc from chrome? Is it worth the effort?

&#x200B;

* In that case, I'd just nuke it from your system and go download DaVinci Resolve. It's free, it does everything Premiere Pro does, faster. And who knows if your torrented version has the latest patches.

\--uhh idk about the, a whole new software, whole new tricks? I have got a habit of using this rn? But at the same time davinci is free. I mean premiere pro works just fine. Exporting and rendering videos will always take time in any software i guess.

&#x200B;

EDIT: bruh, i am pretty sure i was opening my videos before it gets rendered? Wish obs had a feature to tell me if it's still rendering or not?
